What adopting CameraX costs :app's release APK, measured 2026-11-02.

Both sides are :app at release, R8 and resource shrinking on, four ABIs, built on this
machine minutes apart. The baseline is a worktree at dde667cd1, the parent of the adoption
commit; the other side is that tree plus the CameraX backend, with :scanner depending on
camera-core / camera-camera2 / camera-lifecycle 1.6.2 and NOT on camera-view.

                              baseline      camerax        delta
  classes.dex                   752000      1682544      +930544
  res/ entries                      24           24           +0
  CameraX's own .so, 4 ABIs          0       164748      +164748
  CameraX's own .so, 2 ABIs          0        65332       +65332   (arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a)

  lib/arm64-v8a/libimage_processing_util_jni.so    32528
  lib/arm64-v8a/libsurface_util_jni.so              4896
  lib/armeabi-v7a/libimage_processing_util_jni.so  24448
  lib/armeabi-v7a/libsurface_util_jni.so            3460
  lib/x86/libimage_processing_util_jni.so          41276
  lib/x86/libsurface_util_jni.so                    3812
  lib/x86_64/libimage_processing_util_jni.so       49416
  lib/x86_64/libsurface_util_jni.so                 4912

**res/ entries: +0.** That is the whole point of refusing camera-view. The spike measured
camera-view at +273 resource entries and +350,792 bytes, through AppCompat and camera-video;
none of it is here.

**The APK-on-disk figure is NOT quoted, because it was confounded.** The baseline worktree
ran `git submodule update --init --recursive`, which initialised third_party/zxing-cpp/zint;
the main checkout has that nested submodule uninitialised. libzxingnative.so therefore
differs between the two trees by about 542 KB across the two ABIs, for a reason that has
nothing to do with the camera stack. The dex and resource rows above are unaffected by it,
and the CameraX .so rows are read directly out of the APK by name.

**classes.dex is +930,544 here against the spike's +377,808 for the lean flavor.** Two
differences, neither investigated: the spike is on CameraX 1.4.2 and this is 1.6.2, and the
spike's application is one activity while :app is the whole Barcode Scanner app, so R8 has a
different keep surface to work against. Recorded as measured rather than reconciled.
